{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793748626,"nonce":"SlQwS0UzX2X1yGST8I4RAdlF9Sw=","message":"Committed 68b4de44b6f9c8f2fcd38b3808caf07fdddb9c03.\n\nPartial progress on interpreter scalar overhead: construct Undef registers directly with resize_with, and inline the common ZyntaxValue::Int read used by integer arithmetic and comparisons. Other value kinds retain the existing conversion and error path in a separate helper. The register representation remains unchanged; compact slots, register-slot reuse and further copy/drop work are still open.\n\nCode inspection on the NUC shows the old initializer calling ZyntaxValue::clone per added register and copying all 72 bytes. Direct construction writes an 8-byte Undef tag per slot, unrolled four at a time. Ordinary integer reads are now inlined; only the general conversion helper has an out-of-line symbol. Numeric unit tests cover integer boundaries and widths, booleans, floating-point coercions (including NaN/infinity), pointers, and type mismatch diagnostics.\n\nOrdinary release NUC measurements against d11cc252a6409cebaade896304f62abe5f86a795, 15 alternating rounds, affinity 0,2,4,6:\n- Recursive frame, roots off: 155.79 -\u003e 129.72 ns, 1.20x.\n- Recursive frame, roots on: 206.41 -\u003e 182.69 ns, 1.13x.\n- One-symbol frame: 104.34 -\u003e 98.89 ns without roots; 149.14 -\u003e 143.18 ns with roots.\n- 24-site symbol frame: 186.16 -\u003e 129.80 ns without roots, 1.43x; 222.46 -\u003e 174.61 ns with roots, 1.27x.\n- Cold symbol frame: 8819.83 -\u003e 8863.08 ns, essentially unchanged.\n- Scalar loop: 41.68 -\u003e 37.22 ns/iteration, 1.12x. A separate 30-round alternating repeat gives 41.825 -\u003e 37.355 ns; ranges 40.98-42.95 and 36.88-39.81 respectively.\n\nSeparate perf stat runs (ten repeats) report cpu_core retired instructions falling from about 849.6M to 718.1M, and cycles from 196.0M to 169.8M for the scalar test process. These are diagnostic counters, not the timing samples used above.\n\nSeven alternating rounds of all 17 Lua kernels and Python float/fannkuch/nbody_modified at five iterations, LLVM enabled and native library snapshots at default settings. All reference outputs/checksums agree. Geometric-mean baseline/candidate wall ratios: Lua 0.9978, Python 1.0046. Whole-process wall time remains essentially unchanged. No Cargo/rustc ran during or between measured arms; baseline and candidate binaries were built and frozen first. Allocation-audit instrumentation was not enabled in timing binaries. Original NUC checkout and all unrelated tracked/untracked contents were restored and verified; temporary benchmark files were removed after archiving results locally.\n\nRejected experiments are retained in the evidence directory: direct initialization alone improved call-heavy fixtures but slowed the scalar control by about 6%, reproduced across 30 rounds. Keeping preparation out of line did not remove that penalty, so that attribute is not in the final change. The final integer-read specialization reduces actual hot-path conversion/call work and improves the scalar control as well as call-heavy fixtures. The exact cause of the earlier code-generation/layout sensitivity has not been isolated.\n\nEvidence: /private/tmp/zyntax-register-init/nuc/{micro.json,scalar-repeat.json,lua.json,python.json,binary-hashes.json,*initialization.asm,*run-frame.asm,scalar-stat-*.txt,v1/,v2/}; local correctness reports are under /private/tmp/zyntax-register-init/. No reviewed conformance baseline was changed.\n\nFinal validation: two numeric unit tests, 26 focused compiler integration tests, eight targeted NUC tests, 942 local TypeScript fixture/profile checks, and 40 Lua checks passed. Complete pinned official TypeScript corpus: 5948/5948 files, PASS 1151, FAIL 12 (existing), UNSUPPORTED 2234, SKIP 3428, no per-case regressions. Report binary SHA-256 matches the final zynode binary. No baseline refresh. Relevant Clippy with -D warnings, formatting, and git diff --check passed.","files":null}]}